From 0ffbb15603ac202b9a1bdaf65b6b66212e449d54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 18:39:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stage 285: two teachers, so that imitation stops being an
 answer

The loop was circular and it is worth saying plainly: a heuristic that
does not understand the question is called the teacher, the mind is
trained to resemble it, and success is measured as resemblance -
G_reaches_teacher says so literally. The only part that was never
imitation is the reward, which comes from the tape's verdict, and that is
why the policy ends up above its teacher at all.

So there are two judges now, both reading the same tape, neither reading
a label, and sharing no criterion on purpose. Votes counts witnesses.
Return counts how many other mentions carry a value together with the
subject, never looking at how often the address said it. Judges built
from the same quantity would agree everywhere and leave nothing to
arbitrate.

Where they agree BC takes the demonstration. Where they differ there is
no target - two actions cannot both be copied - and the episode is left
to the reward, so the contested items are exactly the ones resemblance
cannot solve.

The bar is not to beat two teachers. Both read one tape and the tape is
the truth here, so where they differ at least one is misreading it and
the mind has to be right more often than either reading alone.
G_arbitration checks precisely that, and NO_DISAGREEMENT is a real
outcome: if the judges never differ, the stage has measured nothing.

280's rollout grew one hook, teacher_fn, so the loop did not have to be
copied. --one-teacher restores the single judge with BC everywhere, the
arm the 0.704 baseline came from.

